; reflexivity of list permutation: every list is a permutation of itself, forall L. Perm(L,L).
; By list induction on L: nil is Perm(nil,nil) by permnil; cons h t is Perm(cons h t, cons h t) by
; permskip h applied to the induction hypothesis Perm(t,t). The first theorem over the new Perm
; predicate (Rel 779, four intro rules nil/skip/swap/trans added to the checker core) -- it opens the
; permutation-relation API that FTA uniqueness is built on (see FTA-UNIQUENESS.md).
(all L (rel 779 L L))
(listind L (rel 779 L L) (permnil) (gen h (gen t (lam ih (rel 779 t t) (permskip h ih)))))
